    },
    "name": {
      "value": "Wand of Rolling Flames (2nd-level Spell)"
    },
    "source": {
      "value": "tv"
    },
    "description": {
      "value": "The luminous design of red-orange cracks on this black obsidian wand suggests cooling lava.\n\n- **Frequency:** once per day\n\nYou cast flaming sphere of the indicated level. The ground in the sphere's square and all adjacent squares are coated in rolling flames until the start of your next turn. These are difficult terrain and hazardous terrain. A creature that moves on the ground takes fire damage for every square of rolling flames it moves into, with the amount determined by the wand's type. If a creature in the flames doesn't move on its turn, it takes the damage for each of the squares it's in at the end of its turn. The first time you Sustain the Spell each round, the sphere creates rolling flames again in its new location (or the same location if you chose not to move it).\n\nThe rolling flames deal 1 fire damage."
    },
